ndlord responds, they use up a card and I can evaluate whether to contest or let teammate take control\n\nReason:\nPlaying ♠3 is the optimal move because: (1) I have free play so I can start with any card, (2) Starting with the weakest card preserves my high cards (A, 2) for critical moments when I need to regain control, (3) With only 7 cards left and the landlord at 6, every card I play brings me closer to victory, (4) If the landlord or teammate plays higher, I can choose to pass and save my strong cards, (5) If both pass, I maintain control and can continue emptying my hand systematically.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠3"]}'}
